From 700f088c201976a04810da464d93d1dca45b8952 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:42:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 141/141] parse/mir: `super let` bindings, owned by the enclosing block

core 1.90's `pin!` expands to

    { super let mut pinned = $value; unsafe { Pin::new_unchecked(&mut pinned) } }

(the unstable `super_let` feature). sad 0.4.32 main.rs:74 `let mut out =
pin!(out);` failed to parse: `super` started a path, "Unexpected token
TOK_RWORD_LET, expected TOK_DOUBLE_COLON". tokio and futures use their
own pin macros, so this is the first user of core's.

A statement beginning `super let` is parsed as a let binding flagged
`m_is_super` (AST) / `m_super` (HIR). In MIR lowering the bindings are
owned by the enclosing variable scope instead of the block's own, so
they are dropped with the enclosing block: the `Pin<&mut T>` returned
from the macro's block stays valid, matching the temporary lifetime
extension rustc applies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
